{%- comment -%}
  A Pinglide map on a Shopify storefront (docs/notes/shopify.md, "Storefront").

  Nothing here calls us when a visitor loads the page (CLAUDE.md §2). Which map
  to show comes from two things the app writes when a map is put on the
  storefront:

  - the "Map" setting, a picker of `$app:map` metaobjects — one per map, with
    `name` (what the picker lists) and `snapshot` (its live snapshot URL). The
    schema has to name the type in full, `app--<app id>--map`: Shopify refuses
    `$app:map` there (it works in Liquid only), so the id is this app's and a
    second app (production) needs its own;
  - the app-data metafield `app.metafields.pinglide.maps`, for the default map
    shown while the picker is empty, and where `map.js` lives:

      { "default": "<mapId>", "script": "https://cdn.pinglide.com/embed/v1/map.js",
        "maps": { "<mapId>": { "name": "…", "snapshot": "https://cdn.pinglide.com/…" } } }

  The page then loads `map.js` and the live snapshot from the CDN, exactly as a
  pasted snippet does. The markup is the WordPress block's (render.php):
  `script[type=text/plain][data-snapshot]` beside a canvas the embed sizes from
  `data-height`. No embed change, so the embed's own-code budget is untouched.

  **The canvas carries an inline `display:block`, and it must.** Dawn and every
  theme built on it ship `div:empty{display:none}`, and the canvas is an empty
  div until the map mounts into it. Hidden, it never intersects the viewport,
  so the embed's lazy loader never starts the map: a blank block on the
  storefront and in the theme editor, which only "Load the map straight away"
  (no wait for the viewport) got past.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign data = app.metafields.pinglide.maps.value
  assign picked = block.settings.map
  assign snapshot = ''
  if picked
    assign snapshot = picked.snapshot.value
  endif
  if snapshot == blank and data.default != blank
    assign snapshot = data.maps[data.default].snapshot
  endif
  assign script_url = data.script | default: 'https://cdn.pinglide.com/embed/v1/map.js'
  assign id = 'pinglide-' | append: block.id
  assign height = block.settings.height | default: 520
  assign phone_height = block.settings.phone_height | default: 420
-%}

{%- if snapshot != blank -%}
  <div
    id="{{ id }}"
    class="pinglide-map{% if block.settings.different_phone_height %} pinglide-map--phone{% endif %}"
    style="--pinglide-height:{{ height }}px;--pinglide-phone-height:{{ phone_height }}px"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <style>
      .pinglide-map{overflow:hidden}
      .pinglide-map__canvas{display:block!important;height:var(--pinglide-height)!important}
      @media (max-width:749px){.pinglide-map--phone .pinglide-map__canvas{height:var(--pinglide-phone-height)!important}}
    </style>
    <script
      type="text/plain"
      data-snapshot="{{ snapshot | escape }}"
      data-target="#{{ id }}-canvas"
      data-height="{{ height }}"
      {%- if block.settings.eager %} data-eager{% endif -%}
    ></script>
    <div id="{{ id }}-canvas" class="pinglide-map__canvas" style="display:block;height:{{ height }}px"></div>
  </div>
  <script type="module" src="{{ script_url | escape }}"></script>
  {%- comment -%}
    Shopify's Customer Privacy API, for the embed's visitor measurement: on a
    Shopify store it sends only when `analyticsProcessingAllowed()` says so,
    and sends nothing while the API is missing (embed/src/track.ts). Loaded
    here because a theme without a cookie banner may never load it. Shopify's
    own script — nothing of ours runs per visitor (CLAUDE.md §2).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    window.Shopify && Shopify.loadFeatures && Shopify.loadFeatures([{ name: "consent-tracking-api", version: "0.2" }], function () {});
  </script>

  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The theme editor re-renders a section in place, and a module runs once,
      so a re-rendered block would stay empty. In the editor only, load map.js
      again under a fresh query string: a new module instance boots every
      `script[data-snapshot]` it has not mounted (embed/src/boot.ts).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function () {
        if (window.__pinglideEditorReboot) return;
        window.__pinglideEditorReboot = true;
        var src = {{ script_url | json }};
        var n = 0;
        document.addEventListener("shopify:section:load", function () {
          n += 1;
          import(src + (src.indexOf("?") < 0 ? "?" : "&") + "r=" + n).catch(function () {});
        });
      })();
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No map on the storefront yet. Merchants see where to go, on a plain card
    that cannot be mistaken for the map (a picture of one was); visitors see
    nothing at all — no empty box with margins on a live page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="pinglide-map pinglide-map--setup"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    style="box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:{{ height }}px;padding:24px;border:1px dashed #b5b8bc;border-radius:8px;background:#f6f6f7;color:#303030;font:14px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:center"
  >
    <div style="max-width:380px">
      <strong style="display:block;margin-bottom:4px;font-size:15px">Choose a map for this block</strong>
      Open Pinglide, pick a map and press <em>Show on storefront</em>. It appears here.
      <a href="https://{{ shop.permanent_domain }}/admin/apps/pinglide/maps" target="_top" style="display:block;margin-top:12px;color:#005bd3">Open Pinglide</a>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Pinglide map",
  "target": "content",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "metaobject",
      "id": "map",
      "label": "Map",
      "metaobject_type": "app--442457194497--map",
      "info": "Empty shows your default map. A map is listed here once you press Show on storefront for it in Pinglide."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height",
      "label": "Height",
      "min": 240,
      "max": 1200,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 520
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "different_phone_height",
      "label": "Use a different height on phones",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "phone_height",
      "label": "Height on phones",
      "min": 240,
      "max": 1200,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 420
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "eager",
      "label": "Load the map straight away",
      "info": "Off, the map loads as visitors scroll near it, which keeps the page fast.",
      "default": false
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
